{% doc %}
  Report a problem — the claim desk.

  Replaces the generic `sv-page` frame for /pages/report-a-problem, which
  rendered 600 words of Admin RTE in a 760px column. That framing was
  wrong for this page in a way it is not wrong for About Us: nobody reads
  this one. They arrive angry, on a phone, inside a 24-hour window,
  holding a video file they do not know how to send. The page has to be
  a task, not an essay.

  So it is built as a flow:

    window   the 24-hour deadline as the first thing on the page
    triage   four claim types; choosing one prefills every send route
             and narrows the kit below to what that claim actually needs
    kit      the three things to send, tickable, held in localStorage so
             leaving for WhatsApp and coming back does not reset them
    film     the unboxing rule, scroll-scrubbed rather than described —
             it is the single reason most claims fail
    routes   WhatsApp / email / large file, each carrying the order
             number and the claim type the visitor has already given us
    next     what happens after, on a rail that draws as it is read
    why      the honest paragraph, in the page's one emerald moment

  Content lives in schema blocks rather than the Admin RTE because the
  triage, the kit filtering, the anchors and the HowTo JSON-LD all need
  structure the RTE cannot carry. Every string, label and toggle is a
  theme-editor setting — nothing here is hard-coded copy.

  Motion contract, per sv-system.css §08: transform and opacity only,
  with two bounded exceptions that file already allows (the disclosure's
  height, and stroke-dashoffset on the line art, which is neither a
  layout property nor unbounded). Scroll-linked motion is CSS
  scroll-driven where the browser has it and IntersectionObserver
  steps where it does not. Nothing on the page needs an animation to
  finish in order to be readable, and every route out — WhatsApp, email,
  the policy links — is a plain anchor that works with script disabled.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign wa = section.settings.whatsapp | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-'
  assign mail = section.settings.email
  assign bg = section.settings.bg_motion

  comment
    Blocks are a flat list; each kind is counted first so a section can be
    skipped whole rather than rendering an empty frame around nothing.
  endcomment
  assign n_claim = 0
  assign n_need = 0
  assign n_frame = 0
  assign n_route = 0
  assign n_step = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    case block.type
      when 'claim'
        assign n_claim = n_claim | plus: 1
      when 'need'
        assign n_need = n_need | plus: 1
      when 'frame'
        assign n_frame = n_frame | plus: 1
      when 'route'
        assign n_route = n_route | plus: 1
      when 'step'
        assign n_step = n_step | plus: 1
    endcase
  endfor

  comment
    The opening line of every prefilled message. Built once here so the
    WhatsApp deep link, the mailto body and the script all agree.
  endcomment
  assign opener = section.settings.prefill_opener
-%}

{{ 'sv-report.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<section class="sv-rp sv-rp--bg-{{ bg }}" data-sv data-sv-report
         style="--sv-rp-frames:{{ n_frame }}">

  {%- render 'sv-motion-gate' -%}


  {%- comment -%}
    ── The ground ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Decorative only: aria-hidden, pointer-events none, carries no
    content. A slow weave, two drifting lights and the brand petal —
    the same vocabulary as the FAQ, so the two support pages read as
    one pair rather than two designs.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless bg == 'off' -%}
    <div class="sv-rp__bg" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="sv-rp__weave"></div>
      <div class="sv-rp__glow sv-rp__glow--a"></div>
      <div class="sv-rp__glow sv-rp__glow--b"></div>
      {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
        <svg class="sv-rp__petal sv-rp__petal--{{ i }}" viewBox="-14 -86 28 92" focusable="false">
          <path d="M0 0 C -9 -30 -6 -62 0 -80 C 6 -62 9 -30 0 0 Z"/>
        </svg>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endunless -%}

  <div class="w sv-rp__inner">

    {%- comment -%}
      ── The thread ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
      One gold stitch running the height of the flow, drawn as the page
      is read. Scroll-driven where the browser has it; the --read
      custom property the script keeps is the fallback, and under
      reduced motion it simply sits at its measured position. It is
      ornament — if it never moves, nothing is lost.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <svg class="sv-rp__thread" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"
         viewBox="0 0 12 1000" preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <path d="M6 0 C 11 120, 1 240, 6 360 C 11 480, 1 600, 6 720 C 11 840, 1 940, 6 1000"/>
    </svg>

    {%- comment -%} ── Masthead ────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="sv-rp__head" data-sv-motion>
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Line reveal, by line — §08 permits no finer grain. The spans are
        always in the markup; only the motion-ready class turns them
        into a mask, so the title is never left hidden if script fails.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h1 class="sv-rp__title">
        <span class="sv-rp__line"><span>{{ section.settings.title_a }}</span></span>
        {%- if section.settings.title_b != blank -%}
          <span class="sv-rp__line"><span>{{ section.settings.title_b }}</span></span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </h1>

      {%- if section.settings.lead != blank -%}
        <p class="sv-rp__lead lead">{{ section.settings.lead }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        ── The window ────────────────────────────────────────────────
        The deadline was a bold word inside a sentence. It is the one
        fact that decides whether a claim is payable, so it gets the
        arc, the scale and the first position on the page.

        The arc is stroke-dashoffset on a single circle — bounded,
        compositor-friendly, and inert with motion reduced.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sv-rp__window">
        <div class="sv-rp__dial" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" focusable="false">
            <circle class="sv-rp__dialtrack" cx="60" cy="60" r="52"/>
            <circle class="sv-rp__dialarc" cx="60" cy="60" r="52"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="sv-rp__dialnum">{{ section.settings.window_value }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="sv-rp__windowtext">
          <p class="lab">{{ section.settings.window_label }}</p>
          <p class="sv-rp__windowline">{{ section.settings.window_line }}</p>
          {%- if section.settings.window_note != blank -%}
            <p class="sv-rp__windownote sv-fine">{{ section.settings.window_note }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The action, at the top. T-099 allows one floating cluster per
        site and the footer already owns it, so this is an in-flow
        button — never a second float.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sv-rp__actions">
        <a class="btn sv-rp__go" data-sv-wa
           href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}?text={{ opener | url_encode }}"
           rel="noopener" target="_blank">{{ section.settings.cta_primary }}</a>
        <a class="act sv-rp__alt" href="#{{ section.settings.routes_slug }}">
          {{ section.settings.cta_secondary }}
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    {%- comment -%}
      ── 01 · Triage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Four buttons, not four bullets. Choosing one is the only input
      the page asks for, and it pays for itself three times: it names
      the claim in every prefilled message, it narrows the kit below to
      what that claim needs, and it tells the visitor in one tap that
      their situation is one we cover.

      They are <button>s inside a list, so keyboard and screen-reader
      users get the same affordance. With script off they are inert —
      which is why nothing below them is hidden by default.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if n_claim > 0 -%}
      <section class="sv-rp__sec sv-rp__triage" id="{{ section.settings.triage_slug }}" data-sv-motion
               aria-labelledby="sv-rp-triage-h">
        <h2 class="sv-rp__h" id="sv-rp-triage-h">{{ section.settings.triage_title }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.triage_note != blank -%}
          <p class="sv-rp__note-lead sv-read">{{ section.settings.triage_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <ul class="sv-rp__claims" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'claim' -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign slug = block.settings.slug | default: block.id | handle
                assign wa_text = block.settings.wa_text | default: block.settings.label
              -%}
              <li class="sv-rp__claimwrap" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <button class="sv-rp__claim" type="button"
                        data-sv-claim="{{ slug }}"
                        data-sv-needs="{{ block.settings.needs | escape }}"
                        data-sv-text="{{ wa_text | escape }}"
                        aria-pressed="false">
                  <span class="sv-rp__claimart" aria-hidden="true">
                    {%- render 'sv-report-icon', art: block.settings.art -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="sv-rp__claimlab">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                  {%- if block.settings.detail != blank -%}
                    <span class="sv-rp__claimdet">{{ block.settings.detail }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="sv-rp__claimtick" aria-hidden="true">
                    <svg viewBox="-14 -86 28 92" focusable="false">
                      <path d="M0 0 C -9 -30 -6 -62 0 -80 C 6 -62 9 -30 0 0 Z"/>
                    </svg>
                  </span>
                </button>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>

        {%- if section.settings.triage_exclusion != blank -%}
          <div class="note sv-rp__exclusion">{{ section.settings.triage_exclusion }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      ── 02 · The kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────
      "What to send us" was a static <ol>. It is the actual task, so it
      is tickable, it counts, and it remembers — a visitor who leaves
      for their camera roll and comes back finds their place.

      The ticks are aria role=checkbox on buttons rather than real
      inputs: there is no form, nothing posts, and a checkbox that
      submits nowhere inside a <form> would be a lie about what the
      page does.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if n_need > 0 -%}
      <section class="sv-rp__sec sv-rp__kit" id="{{ section.settings.kit_slug }}" data-sv-motion
               aria-labelledby="sv-rp-kit-h">
        <h2 class="sv-rp__h" id="sv-rp-kit-h">{{ section.settings.kit_title }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.kit_note != blank -%}
          <p class="sv-rp__note-lead sv-read">{{ section.settings.kit_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="sv-rp__kitgrid">
          <ol class="sv-rp__needs" data-sv-needs>
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'need' -%}
                {%- assign nslug = block.settings.slug | default: block.id | handle -%}
                <li class="sv-rp__need" data-sv-need="{{ nslug }}"
                    data-sv-for="{{ block.settings.claims | escape }}"
                    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <button class="sv-rp__tick" type="button" role="checkbox" aria-checked="false"
                          data-sv-tick="{{ nslug }}">
                    <span class="sv-rp__tickmark" aria-hidden="true">
                      <svg viewBox="-14 -86 28 92" focusable="false">
                        <path d="M0 0 C -9 -30 -6 -62 0 -80 C 6 -62 9 -30 0 0 Z"/>
                      </svg>
                    </span>
                    <span class="sv-visually-hidden">{{ section.settings.tick_label }}</span>
                  </button>

                  <div class="sv-rp__needbody">
                    <p class="sv-rp__needlab sv-read-lab">{{ block.settings.label }}</p>
                    {%- if block.settings.detail != blank -%}
                      <div class="sv-rp__needdet sv-read">{{ block.settings.detail }}</div>
                    {%- endif -%}

                    {%- comment -%}
                      The hint is a real <details>, so it works with no
                      script at all. Where the browser has
                      interpolate-size the open and close are animated;
                      where it does not, it simply snaps — which is what
                      <details> has always done.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- if block.settings.hint != blank -%}
                      <details class="sv-rp__hint">
                        <summary class="sv-rp__hintsum">
                          <span>{{ block.settings.hint_label | default: 'Where do I find this?' }}</span>
                        </summary>
                        <div class="sv-rp__hintbody sv-read">{{ block.settings.hint }}</div>
                      </details>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ol>

          {%- comment -%}
            ── The gauge ───────────────────────────────────────────────
            The ring, the order-number field and the armed button. The
            field is not a form control in the posting sense — it exists
            so the order number can ride along in the WhatsApp and email
            links, which is the one thing that actually speeds a claim up
            at our end.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <aside class="sv-rp__gauge" data-sv-gauge>
            <div class="sv-rp__ring" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" focusable="false">
                <circle class="sv-rp__ringtrack" cx="60" cy="60" r="50"/>
                <circle class="sv-rp__ringarc" cx="60" cy="60" r="50"/>
              </svg>
              <span class="sv-rp__ringnum" data-sv-count>0/{{ n_need }}</span>
            </div>

            <p class="sv-rp__gaugestate" data-sv-state role="status">
              {{ section.settings.gauge_waiting }}
            </p>

            <div class="sv-rp__field">
              <label class="sv-rp__fieldlab sv-read-lab" for="sv-rp-order">
                {{ section.settings.order_label }}
              </label>
              <input class="sv-rp__input" id="sv-rp-order" type="text" inputmode="text"
                     autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                     placeholder="{{ section.settings.order_placeholder | escape }}"
                     data-sv-order>
              <p class="sv-rp__fieldnote sv-fine">{{ section.settings.order_note }}</p>
            </div>

            <a class="btn sv-rp__go sv-rp__go--gauge" data-sv-wa
               href="https://wa.me/{{ wa }}?text={{ opener | url_encode }}"
               rel="noopener" target="_blank">{{ section.settings.cta_primary }}</a>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ── 03 · The film ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    The unboxing rule, shown rather than described. It sits outside the
    measured column because it is the one full-bleed moment on the page.

    The stage is sticky and the scrub below it supplies the scroll
    length. Where the browser has scroll-driven animations the frames
    cross-fade continuously and reverse on the way back up, with no
    script at all; where it does not, the script steps them with an
    observer. Under reduced motion the whole thing unstacks into four
    plain captioned figures — which is the same information, told
    without movement.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if n_frame > 0 -%}
    <section class="sv-rp__film" id="{{ section.settings.film_slug }}"
             aria-labelledby="sv-rp-film-h">
      <div class="sv-rp__filmtrack">
        <div class="w sv-rp__filminner">

          <div class="sv-rp__filmcopy">
            <p class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.film_eyebrow }}</p>
            <h2 class="sv-rp__h sv-rp__filmh" id="sv-rp-film-h">{{ section.settings.film_title }}</h2>

            <ol class="sv-rp__caps" data-sv-caps>
              {%- assign fi = 0 -%}
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'frame' -%}
                  {%- assign fi = fi | plus: 1 -%}
                  <li class="sv-rp__cap{% if fi == 1 %} is-on{% endif %}"
                      data-sv-cap="{{ fi }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="num sv-rp__capnum">{{ fi }}</span>
                    <span class="sv-rp__captitle">{{ block.settings.caption }}</span>
                    {%- if block.settings.detail != blank -%}
                      <span class="sv-rp__capdet sv-read">{{ block.settings.detail }}</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ol>

            <div class="sv-rp__pips" data-sv-pips aria-hidden="true">
              {%- for i in (1..n_frame) -%}
                <i class="{% if forloop.first %}on{% endif %}"></i>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sv-rp__stage">
            {%- assign si = 0 -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'frame' -%}
                {%- assign si = si | plus: 1 -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A photograph wins over the drawing when one is set, and
                  the drawing stays as the fallback rather than being
                  replaced — so a frame whose image has not been uploaded
                  yet still renders a scene rather than a hole, and the
                  sequence can be filled in one frame at a time.

                  alt is empty by design: the figcaption below already
                  names the frame, and the caption list beside the stage
                  carries the same words again. A third reading of it
                  would be noise in a screen reader, not help.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <figure class="sv-rp__scene{% if block.settings.image != blank %} sv-rp__scene--img{% endif %}{% if si == 1 %} is-on{% endif %}"
                        data-sv-scene="{{ si }}" style="--sv-rp-i:{{ si }}">
                  {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      ── Loading ──────────────────────────────────────
                      The first frame is not lazy. Once the sequence
                      pins it is the whole screen, and a lazy image only
                      begins loading as it nears the viewport — which on
                      this page is the same moment it is needed, so it
                      arrived visibly late every time.

                      Frames two to four stay lazy. They are absolutely
                      positioned inside the same stage, so the browser
                      starts fetching them as soon as that stage enters
                      the viewport — roughly a full viewport of scroll
                      before the scrub reaches them, and each is about
                      100KB over a warm CDN.

                      ── sizes ────────────────────────────────────────
                      Measured rather than guessed. The old 46vw was
                      wrong at every width and made the browser pick a
                      larger file than it could ever use:

                        .w caps at 1220 with 48px of padding  → 1124
                        filminner is 5fr 7fr with a 72px gap  → 1052
                        the stage is the 7fr column           → ~614px

                      So above 1220 the stage is a fixed 614px and does
                      not scale with the viewport at all. Below 881 it
                      unstacks to the full column, and below 760 the
                      page padding drops to 28px a side.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign img_loading = 'lazy'
                      assign img_priority = 'auto'
                      if si == 1
                        assign img_loading = 'eager'
                        assign img_priority = 'high'
                      endif
                    -%}
                    {{
                      block.settings.image
                      | image_url: width: 1600
                      | image_tag:
                        loading: img_loading,
                        fetchpriority: img_priority,
                        decoding: 'async',
                        sizes: '(min-width: 1220px) 614px, (min-width: 881px) calc(58.3vw - 98px), (min-width: 761px) calc(100vw - 96px), calc(100vw - 56px)',
                        widths: '400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1600',
                        class: 'sv-rp__photo',
                        alt: ''
                    }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- render 'sv-report-scene', art: block.settings.art -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <figcaption class="sv-visually-hidden">{{ block.settings.caption }}</figcaption>
                </figure>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The scroll length. One viewport per frame — the sticky track
        above it holds while this passes. It carries nothing, so on a
        narrow screen and under reduced motion it collapses to zero and
        the stage becomes an ordinary stack.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sv-rp__scrub" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      {%- if section.settings.film_note != blank -%}
        <div class="w sv-rp__filmfoot" data-sv-motion>
          <div class="note sv-rp__filmnote">{{ section.settings.film_note }}</div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="w sv-rp__inner sv-rp__inner--b">

    {%- comment -%}
      ── 04 · Routes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Three ways to reach us, each carrying whatever the visitor has
      already told the page. Every one is a plain anchor with a working
      href before script touches it.

      There is deliberately no upload form here. Shopify's contact form
      cannot take a 400MB video, and offering a field that silently
      fails on the file the whole claim depends on would be worse than
      offering nothing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if n_route > 0 -%}
      <section class="sv-rp__sec sv-rp__routes" id="{{ section.settings.routes_slug }}" data-sv-motion
               aria-labelledby="sv-rp-routes-h">
        <h2 class="sv-rp__h" id="sv-rp-routes-h">{{ section.settings.routes_title }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.routes_note != blank -%}
          <p class="sv-rp__note-lead sv-read">{{ section.settings.routes_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <ul class="sv-rp__routelist" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'route' -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign kind = block.settings.kind
                assign href = ''

                comment
                  The opener is encoded on its own line. Chained onto the
                  append it would encode the scheme and the number too,
                  and wa.me would be handed one long literal.
                endcomment
                assign opener_enc = opener | url_encode

                case kind
                  when 'whatsapp'
                    assign href = 'https://wa.me/' | append: wa | append: '?text=' | append: opener_enc
                  when 'email'
                    assign href = 'mailto:' | append: mail
                  else
                    assign href = block.settings.url
                endcase
              -%}
              <li class="sv-rp__route sv-rp__route--{{ kind }}{% if block.settings.primary %} is-primary{% endif %}"
                  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="sv-rp__routeart" aria-hidden="true">
                  {%- render 'sv-report-icon', art: kind -%}
                </span>

                <h3 class="sv-rp__routeh">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
                {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
                  <div class="sv-rp__routebody sv-read">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if kind == 'note' -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    A route with nowhere to click — the large-file
                    advice. It keeps the card so the three read as one
                    row rather than two cards and a paragraph.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- elsif href != blank -%}
                  <a class="{% if block.settings.primary %}btn{% else %}btn btn--ghost{% endif %} sv-rp__routego"
                     {% if kind == 'whatsapp' %}data-sv-wa{% elsif kind == 'email' %}data-sv-mail{% endif %}
                     href="{{ href }}"
                     {% if kind != 'email' %}rel="noopener" target="_blank"{% endif %}>
                    {{ block.settings.cta | default: 'Open' }}
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if kind == 'email' -%}
                  <p class="sv-rp__copy">
                    <span class="sv-rp__copyval" data-sv-copyval>{{ mail }}</span>
                    <button class="sv-rp__copybtn" type="button" data-sv-copy="{{ mail }}" hidden>
                      <span data-sv-copytext>{{ section.settings.copy_label }}</span>
                    </button>
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      ── 05 · What happens next ──────────────────────────────────────
      A rail rather than a bulleted list, because the value of this
      section is that it is a sequence with times attached. The
      connecting line scales with scroll where the browser has
      scroll-driven animation, and is simply drawn where it does not.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if n_step > 0 -%}
      <section class="sv-rp__sec sv-rp__next" id="{{ section.settings.next_slug }}" data-sv-motion
               aria-labelledby="sv-rp-next-h">
        <h2 class="sv-rp__h" id="sv-rp-next-h">{{ section.settings.next_title }}</h2>

        <ol class="sv-rp__rail">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'step' -%}
              <li class="sv-rp__stop" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="sv-rp__stopdot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                {%- if block.settings.meta != blank -%}
                  <span class="lab sv-rp__stopmeta">{{ block.settings.meta }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <h3 class="sv-rp__stoph">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
                {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}
                  <div class="sv-rp__stopbody sv-read">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ol>

        {%- if section.settings.next_note != blank -%}
          <div class="note sv-rp__nextnote">{{ section.settings.next_note }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </section>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    ── 06 · Why ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    The one inverted moment the system allows per page (§07). It goes
    to the video paragraph because that paragraph is the page arguing
    its own case, and it is the best writing on the site.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.why_quote != blank or section.settings.why_body != blank -%}
    <aside class="sv-rp__why panel-dark" data-sv-motion aria-labelledby="sv-rp-why-h">
      <div class="w n sv-rp__whyinner">
        <p class="lab">{{ section.settings.why_label }}</p>
        <h2 class="sv-rp__whyh" id="sv-rp-why-h">{{ section.settings.why_title }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.why_quote != blank -%}
          <div class="pull sv-rp__pull">
            <p>{{ section.settings.why_quote }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.why_body != blank -%}
          <div class="sv-rp__whybody">{{ section.settings.why_body }}</div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </aside>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ── 07 · The small print ──────────────────────────────────────────
    The page is a summary and says so. These links are the reason it is
    allowed to be one.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.fine != blank -%}
    <div class="w sv-rp__inner sv-rp__fine" data-sv-motion>
      <div class="sv-rp__finebody sv-read">{{ section.settings.fine }}</div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ── HowTo ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    The kit and the routes are literally a procedure, so the page is
    eligible for HowTo rather than the FAQPage the FAQ emits. Built from
    the real blocks, so it can never drift from what is on screen.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if n_need > 0 -%}
    {%- capture howto_steps -%}
      {%- assign hi = 0 -%}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.type == 'need' -%}
          {%- assign hi = hi | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- if hi > 1 %},{% endif -%}
          {
            "@type": "HowToStep",
            "position": {{ hi }},
            "name": {{ block.settings.label | strip_html | json }},
            "text": {{ block.settings.detail | strip_html | strip_newlines | json }}
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":{{ section.settings.title_a | append: ' ' | append: section.settings.title_b | strip_html | json }},"description":{{ section.settings.lead | strip_html | json }},"step":[{{ howto_steps | strip_newlines }}]}
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}

  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('[data-sv-report]');
      if (!root) return;

      var calm = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
      root.classList.add('sv-rp--js');

      /* ── Sticky offset ──────────────────────────────────────────────
         The gauge parks under the header group, and a pasted anchor has
         to land clear of it. That height is not knowable in CSS — it
         changes with the announcement bar and between breakpoints — so
         it is measured. The CSS fallback value stands until it is. */
      var chrome = document.getElementById('header-group');
      function setStick() {
        if (!chrome) return;
        var h = Math.round(chrome.getBoundingClientRect().height);
        if (h > 0) root.style.setProperty('--stick', h + 'px');
      }
      setStick();
      window.addEventListener('resize', setStick);

      var WA    = {{ wa | json }};
      var MAIL  = {{ mail | json }};
      var OPEN  = {{ opener | json }};
      var SUBJ  = {{ section.settings.mail_subject | json }};
      var STATE = {
        waiting: {{ section.settings.gauge_waiting | json }},
        part:    {{ section.settings.gauge_part | json }},
        ready:   {{ section.settings.gauge_ready | json }}
      };

      var store = {
        get: function (k) { try { return window.localStorage.getItem('sv-rp:' + k); } catch (e) { return null; } },
        set: function (k, v) { try { window.localStorage.setItem('sv-rp:' + k, v); } catch (e) {} },
        del: function (k) { try { window.localStorage.removeItem('sv-rp:' + k); } catch (e) {} }
      };

      /* ── Shared state ───────────────────────────────────────────────
         One object, one writer. Everything that can change a link —
         the claim, the ticks, the order number — funnels through
         paint(), so the WhatsApp deep link at the top of the page and
         the one in the gauge can never disagree. */
      var claim = null;       /* { slug, text, needs } */
      var order = '';
      var ticked = Object.create(null);

      var claimBtns = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-claim]'));
      var needs     = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-need]'));
      var tickBtns  = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-tick]'));
      var waLinks   = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-wa]'));
      var mailLinks = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-mail]'));
      var countEl   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-count]');
      var stateEl   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-state]');
      var gauge     = root.querySelector('[data-sv-gauge]');
      var orderEl   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-order]');

      /* ── Message ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Composed rather than templated, so an empty field simply drops
         its clause instead of leaving "order number: " hanging. */
      function message() {
        var out = OPEN;
        if (claim && claim.text) out += ' ' + claim.text + '.';
        if (order) out += ' Order ' + order + '.';
        return out;
      }

      function paint() {
        var msg = message();
        waLinks.forEach(function (a) {
          a.href = 'https://wa.me/' + WA + '?text=' + encodeURIComponent(msg);
        });
        mailLinks.forEach(function (a) {
          var subject = SUBJ + (order ? ' — ' + order : '');
          a.href = 'mailto:' + MAIL +
            '?subject=' + encodeURIComponent(subject) +
            '&body=' + encodeURIComponent(msg);
        });
      }

      /* ── Triage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Selecting a claim narrows the kit. A need with no claim list
         belongs to every claim; one that names claims appears only for
         those. Nothing is ever removed from the DOM — hidden items
         come back the moment the claim changes or is cleared. */
      function applyClaim(next) {
        claim = next;
        root.setAttribute('data-sv-picked', next ? next.slug : '');

        claimBtns.forEach(function (b) {
          var on = !!next && b.dataset.svClaim === next.slug;
          b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
          b.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
        });

        needs.forEach(function (li) {
          var only = (li.dataset.svFor || '').trim();
          var show = true;
          if (next && only) {
            show = only.split(',').some(function (s) { return s.trim() === next.slug; });
          }
          li.hidden = !show;
        });

        tally();
        paint();
      }

      /* A DOM change that reorders visible items is exactly what the
         View Transitions API is for. Where it is absent — or motion is
         reduced — the mutation simply happens, which is the same
         result without the cross-fade. */
      function transition(mutate) {
        if (calm || !document.startViewTransition) { mutate(); return; }
        try { document.startViewTransition(mutate); } catch (e) { mutate(); }
      }

      claimBtns.forEach(function (b) {
        b.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var slug = b.dataset.svClaim;
          var next = (claim && claim.slug === slug) ? null : {
            slug: slug,
            text: b.dataset.svText || '',
            needs: b.dataset.svNeeds || ''
          };
          transition(function () { applyClaim(next); });
          if (next) store.set('claim', slug); else store.del('claim');
        });
      });

      /* ── The kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Ticks are per-browser and survive the trip to WhatsApp and
         back, which is the whole point: the camera roll is a different
         app, and coming back to a reset list reads as lost work. */
      tickBtns.forEach(function (b) {
        var key = b.dataset.svTick;
        if (store.get('tick:' + key) === '1') mark(b, true);

        b.addEventListener('click', function () {
          mark(b, b.getAttribute('aria-checked') !== 'true');
          store.set('tick:' + key, ticked[key] ? '1' : '0');
          tally();
        });
      });

      function mark(b, on) {
        ticked[b.dataset.svTick] = on;
        b.setAttribute('aria-checked', on ? 'true' : 'false');
        b.closest('[data-sv-need]').classList.toggle('is-done', on);
      }

      /* The ring is driven by a registered custom property, so the fill
         interpolates rather than jumping. Where @property is absent the
         value still lands — it simply arrives in one step. */
      function tally() {
        var live = needs.filter(function (li) { return !li.hidden; });
        var done = live.filter(function (li) {
          return ticked[li.dataset.svNeed];
        }).length;
        var total = live.length;

        if (countEl) countEl.textContent = done + '/' + total;
        if (gauge) {
          gauge.style.setProperty('--sv-rp-p', total ? (done / total).toFixed(4) : 0);
          gauge.classList.toggle('is-ready', total > 0 && done === total);
        }

        if (stateEl) {
          var txt = !done ? STATE.waiting : (done === total ? STATE.ready : STATE.part);
          /* role=status announces on change only; writing the same
             string back would be silent anyway, but skipping it keeps
             the node from churning on every unrelated tally. */
          if (stateEl.textContent.trim() !== txt) stateEl.textContent = txt;
        }
      }

      /* ── Order number ───────────────────────────────────────────────
         Never sent anywhere by this page. It is held locally and
         pasted into the message the visitor themselves sends. */
      if (orderEl) {
        var saved = store.get('order');
        if (saved) { orderEl.value = saved; order = saved; }

        orderEl.addEventListener('input', function () {
          order = orderEl.value.trim();
          store.set('order', order);
          paint();
        });
      }

      /* ── Copy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Revealed only where the API exists, so the button is never a
         control that cannot work. */
      var copyBtn = root.querySelector('[data-sv-copy]');
      if (copyBtn && navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
        copyBtn.hidden = false;
        var copyText = copyBtn.querySelector('[data-sv-copytext]');
        var was = copyText ? copyText.textContent : '';
        copyBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(copyBtn.dataset.svCopy).then(function () {
            if (!copyText) return;
            copyText.textContent = {{ section.settings.copy_done | json }};
            copyBtn.classList.add('is-done');
            setTimeout(function () {
              copyText.textContent = was;
              copyBtn.classList.remove('is-done');
            }, 2000);
          }).catch(function () {});
        });
      }

      /* Restore the claim last, so the kit is filtered before the
         first tally rather than counting rows that are about to go. */
      var priorClaim = store.get('claim');
      if (priorClaim) {
        var match = claimBtns.filter(function (b) { return b.dataset.svClaim === priorClaim; })[0];
        if (match) {
          applyClaim({ slug: priorClaim, text: match.dataset.svText || '', needs: match.dataset.svNeeds || '' });
        } else {
          tally();
        }
      } else {
        tally();
      }
      paint();

      /* ── The film ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
         The stylesheet ships a readable baseline — a captioned drawing
         over a numbered list — and the pinned sequence is opted into
         from here, never assumed. Two mechanisms:

           scrub   CSS scroll-driven, continuous and reversible. Its
                   keyframes divide the range into four, which CSS
                   cannot do arithmetically, so it is used only at the
                   count those keyframes are written for.
           step    an observer stepping sentinels across the scrub.
                   Index-driven, so correct at any count.

         Under reduced motion neither is added and the baseline stands.
         The scrub needs no script beyond the class; the step path
         builds its sentinels below. */
      var film = root.querySelector('.sv-rp__film');
      var supportsScrub = !!(window.CSS && CSS.supports && CSS.supports('animation-timeline: view()'));
      var frames = film ? film.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-scene]').length : 0;

      if (film && !calm && frames > 1) {
        if (supportsScrub && frames === 4) {
          root.classList.add('sv-rp--scrub');
        } else if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
          root.classList.add('sv-rp--step');

          var scenes = Array.prototype.slice.call(film.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-scene]'));
          var caps   = Array.prototype.slice.call(film.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-cap]'));
          var pips   = Array.prototype.slice.call(film.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-pips] i'));
          var scrub  = film.querySelector('.sv-rp__scrub');

          if (scrub) {
            var marks = [];
            for (var i = 0; i < scenes.length; i++) {
              var s = document.createElement('i');
              s.className = 'sv-rp__mark';
              s.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
              scrub.appendChild(s);
              marks.push(s);
            }

            var show = function (n) {
              scenes.forEach(function (el, k) { el.classList.toggle('is-on', k === n); });
              caps.forEach(function (el, k) { el.classList.toggle('is-on', k === n); });
              pips.forEach(function (el, k) { el.classList.toggle('on', k === n); });
            };

            var spy = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
              entries.forEach(function (en) {
                if (!en.isIntersecting) return;
                var n = marks.indexOf(en.target);
                if (n > -1) show(n);
              });
            }, { rootMargin: '-50% 0px -50% 0px', threshold: 0 });

            marks.forEach(function (m) { spy.observe(m); });
          }
        }
      }

      /* ── Reveal on scroll ───────────────────────────────────────────
         Same contract as sv-faq and sv-size-guide: fires once, then
         unobserves, and a timer pins each entrance to its finished
         state shortly after it should have arrived. Nothing on this
         page may depend on a transition completing in order to be
         read, and a throttled tab does not advance transitions. */
      if (!calm && 'IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        root.classList.add('sv-motion-ready');

        var held = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]'));

        var pinEntrance = function (el) {
          setTimeout(function () { el.classList.add('sv-settled'); }, 1800);
        };

        var reveal = function (el) {
          if (el.classList.contains('sv-vis')) return;
          el.classList.add('sv-vis');
          mo.unobserve(el);
          pinEntrance(el);
        };

        var mo = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
          entries.forEach(function (en) { if (en.isIntersecting) reveal(en.target); });
        }, { rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px', threshold: 0.06 });

        held.forEach(function (el) { mo.observe(el); });

        /* The masthead is above the fold by definition. Waiting on an
           observer to confirm what is already on screen buys nothing
           but a chance of a blank hero. */
        root.querySelectorAll('.sv-rp__head').forEach(reveal);

        /* An observer reports a state, not every state an element
           passed through. Scroll hard enough in one gesture and a
           section can go from below the fold to above it without a
           callback ever seeing it intersect — and it would then stay
           invisible for good. The sweep closes that. */
        var queued = false;
        var sweep = function () {
          queued = false;
          var fold = window.innerHeight;
          held.forEach(function (el) {
            if (!el.classList.contains('sv-vis') &&
                el.getBoundingClientRect().top < fold) reveal(el);
          });
        };

        window.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
          if (queued) return;
          queued = true;
          setTimeout(sweep, 180);
        }, { passive: true });

        setTimeout(sweep, 1200);
      }

      /* ── The thread ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Ornament, so unlike the reveal it is allowed to lean on rAF:
         if a frame never comes the stitch simply does not move and
         nothing becomes unreadable. Skipped entirely where CSS is
         already driving it. */
      if (!supportsScrub) {
        var inner = root.querySelector('.sv-rp__inner');
        var ticking = false;

        /* rAF must be called with window as its receiver — handing the
           bare function reference around throws Illegal invocation. */
        var frame = window.requestAnimationFrame
          ? window.requestAnimationFrame.bind(window)
          : function (fn) { return setTimeout(fn, 16); };

        var track = function () {
          ticking = false;
          if (!inner) return;
          var r = inner.getBoundingClientRect();
          var seen = window.innerHeight - r.top;
          var read = r.height > 0 ? seen / r.height : 0;
          root.style.setProperty('--sv-rp-read', Math.max(0, Math.min(1, read)).toFixed(4));
        };

        window.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
          if (ticking) return;
          ticking = true;
          frame(track);
        }, { passive: true });

        track();
      }

      /* ── Deep links ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Support pastes /pages/report-a-problem#unboxing into a reply
         and the customer lands on that section, flagged. */
      function land() {
        var id = decodeURIComponent(window.location.hash.slice(1));
        if (!id) return;
        var el = root.querySelector('#' + (window.CSS && CSS.escape ? CSS.escape(id) : id));
        if (!el) return;
        el.scrollIntoView({ block: 'start', behavior: calm ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
        el.classList.add('is-landed');
        setTimeout(function () { el.classList.remove('is-landed'); }, 2200);
      }
      window.addEventListener('hashchange', land);
      if (window.location.hash) setTimeout(land, 60);
    })();
  </script>

</section>


